---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy | The Open Road Foundation"
  description="What we collect, why, and what we do not do with it."
>
  <PageHero
    heading="Privacy"
    lede="Short version: we collect what you type into our form or give with your gift, we use it to reply to you and send your receipt, and we do not sell it."
  />

  <!-- On the .split spine like every other page. This was one long .measure
       column: a 38rem strip on a 72rem page, the same emptiness the mission
       block had. Each heading now sits in the left rail with its own text
       beside it, which also makes a long policy page scannable. -->
  <section class="section surface-base">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="updated reveal">Last updated 22 September 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section--minor surface-base">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split prose">
        <h2 class="reveal">What we collect</h2>
        <p>
          If you fill in our interest form, we receive your name, your email address, the option you
          picked from the dropdown, and whatever you write in the message box. If you tick the
          newsletter box, we record that too.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you give, Givebutter passes us your name, your email address and the amount of your
          gift.
        </p>
        <p>
          We do not run the scholarship application on this site. Essay contest entries are taken
          elsewhere, and this site never receives them.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section--minor surface-panel">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split prose">
        <h2 class="reveal">Why we collect it</h2>
        <p>
          To reply to you, to send your receipt if you give, and to tell you when something
          happens that you asked to hear about. That's all we use it for.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section--minor surface-base">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split prose">
        <h2 class="reveal">Who else sees it</h2>
        <p>
          Three companies, and nobody else. <strong>Formspree</strong> receives what you type into
          our form and passes it on to us by email. <strong>Vercel</strong> hosts this site and
          sees what any web server sees: which pages were asked for, and the address that asked.
        </p>
        <p>
          We run no analytics. Nobody is counting your visit, and nothing here follows you once
          you leave.
        </p>
        <p>
          Gifts are made on <strong>Givebutter</strong>, not on this site. Givebutter and its
          payment processor handle your payment details and pass us your name, email address and
          the amount, so we can send your receipt and thank you. We never see your full card
          number. Givebutter's own privacy policy covers what happens on its pages.
        </p>
        <p>We do not sell or share your details.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section--minor surface-panel">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split prose">
        <h2 class="reveal">How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
          We keep what you send us for as long as we are still in touch about it, and no longer
          than two years. If you are on the newsletter, we keep your email address until you
          unsubscribe, and we delete it after that.
        </p>
        <p>
          Records of a gift are kept for seven years, under our document retention policy.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section--minor surface-base">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split prose">
        <h2 class="reveal">Asking us to delete it</h2>
        <p>
          Email <a href="mailto:openroadfdn.admin@gmail.com">openroadfdn.admin@gmail.com</a> and
          we will remove you. You do not have to give a reason. Records of a gift are the one
          exception: we keep those for seven years, and remove you from everything else.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section--minor surface-panel">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split prose">
        <h2 class="reveal">Children</h2>
        <p>
          Students under 18 are welcome to contact us through the form. We ask for no more than a
          name and an email address, and we do not knowingly collect anything else about a minor on
          this site.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The "full privacy policy replaces this stub" placeholder was removed
       here rather than filled. The page is not a stub: it covers what we
       collect, why, who else sees it, how long we keep it, how to have it
       deleted, and minors. That is a complete policy for a site whose only
       input is a name, an email, a dropdown value and a message.

       Counsel review remains a should-do, not a launch blocker, and becomes one
       the moment the form collects more than it does today. The sentence that
       has to survive any such change is in "Children" above: under-18s may
       contact us and we take no more than a name and an email from them. -->
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .updated {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--fg-quiet);
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
